---
import Layout from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Why I write Ryan's Snowball and how it's built."
	pubDate={new Date('September 02 2026')}
	lang="en"
	hasTranslation={true}
>
	<p>
		Hi, I'm Ryan. <strong>I've been posting to this blog with Claude Code since September 2, 2026.</strong>
		Instead of letting the things I learn while working and living day to day just slip away, I
		collect them, refine them, and pile them up here.
	</p>

	<p>
		The way I write is a bit unusual, too. I normally keep notes in <strong>Obsidian</strong> as a
		personal wiki, and <strong>Claude Code</strong> picks out the notes that are ready, reworks them
		into blog-post tone, and publishes them automatically. The source notes live in a private
		Obsidian vault; the finished posts deploy straight through Vercel. All I really do is keep the
		wiki organized and decide what's ready to ship — and the pipeline itself often becomes a topic
		here, too.
	</p>

	<p>Here's what I mostly write about:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>AI agent automation</strong> — designing, building, and shipping projects with Claude Code</li>
		<li><strong>Algorithmic trading</strong> — building and validating auto-trading bots</li>
		<li><strong>Physical AI & autonomous driving</strong> — Tesla, NVIDIA, and other trends I follow closely</li>
		<li><strong>Knowledge auto-publishing pipeline</strong> — the tools and workflow behind turning notes into posts</li>
	</ul>

	<p>
		This isn't a grand plan — the first goal is just to keep what I've learned so I can find it
		again myself later. If it happens to help someone else looking for the same thing, even better.
	</p>
</Layout>
